# PatternFly Color Semantics (PF 6.x)

Reference: https://www.patternfly.org/ai/guidelines/color/#color-associations-and-statuses

Always apply these color associations when choosing Label colors, status indicators, icons, and severity styling:

| Meaning              | Color token / PF color | Use case                                          |
|----------------------|------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Success / Ready      | `green`                | Fully enabled, healthy, action succeeded          |
| Neutral / N/A        | `grey`                 | Unavailable, not installed, no severity           |
| Info / Note          | `purple`               | Helpful information, previously-visited links     |
| Warning              | `yellow` / `gold`      | Act now to avoid error — non-critical             |
| Caution              | `orange`               | Non-destructive fixable error                     |
| Danger / Critical    | `red`                  | Destructive action, critical error, degraded      |
| Link / Interaction   | blue (default PF link) | Buttons, links, interactive elements              |

## Rules

- ✅ Use `color="green"` + `CheckCircleIcon` for Ready / Fully enabled / Success states.
- ✅ Use `color="grey"` for Not installed, unavailable, or neutral states — **not** `gold`/`yellow`.
- ✅ Use `color="red"` + `ExclamationCircleIcon` for Degraded / Critical / Danger states.
- ✅ Use `color="gold"` or `color="orange"` **only** for Warning / Caution states that require user action to avoid an error.
- ❌ Never use `color="gold"` for "Partial setup" — that is a neutral/grey state (configuration incomplete, not a warning).
- ❌ Never use red/orange/yellow for informational or "not yet installed" states.
- ❌ Never use color to indicate AI features — AI uses the same colors as the rest of the interface.

## Label examples

```tsx
// ✅ Ready / fully enabled
<Label color="green" icon={<CheckCircleIcon />}>Ready</Label>

// ✅ Not installed (neutral)
<Label color="grey">Not installed</Label>

// ✅ Partial setup (neutral — configuration incomplete, not an error)
<Label color="grey">Partial setup</Label>

// ✅ Degraded / critical
<Label color="red" icon={<ExclamationCircleIcon />}>Degraded</Label>

// ✅ Warning — user must act to avoid failure
<Label color="gold" icon={<ExclamationTriangleIcon />}>Needs attention</Label>
```
